+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "  toolChoice: 'required',",
+  "cause": "The refundAgent sets toolChoice to 'required', which forces the model to make a tool call on every turn, so after approveRefund returns a decline it cannot send a plain-text reply and instead re-requests approval, keeps calling lookupOrder, or runs out of turns.",
+  "evidence": "Running refundAgent.chat() on 'I want a refund for order A-1001, it arrived broken.' with approveRefund answered {approved: false} gave finishReason 'interrupted' and a new approveRefund tool request with the original toolChoice; with toolChoice 'auto' the same run ends with finishReason 'stop' and the text 'I'm sorry, your refund for order A-1001 was not approved. A refund was already filed for this order.'"
+}
